     "result_text_tail": "ed without a review round.\n- **\"On the way to $40M by 2030\":** I read this as $40M in 2030. The deck shows Amazon-led reaching two-thirds of it ($26.4M) and suggests the board treat about $26M as the 2030 target, with retail as the next step.\n- **Modelling rules not set by the pack:**\n  - One-time costs are expensed in the year they occur.\n  - Retail units are doors \u00d7 units per door per week \u00d7 52.\n  - Japan's cash equals its operating result, because the pack has no inventory data for it.\n\n**Limits to know about:**\n- I couldn't look at the slides as images: there is no LibreOffice here and the sandbox blocks Keynote. I checked layout through the renderer's warnings and read back every slide's text, so please flip through it once in PowerPoint.\n- The pack gives no Amazon storage or return fees and no currency sensitivity, so neither is modelled. Both are noted on the slides.\n- **One QA warning remains:** the pack says inventory is \"four months\" in words, so the check can't match the number 4 against the quoted text. The figure is right.\n- The web re-check script wasn't needed, since every number comes from the briefing pack. 215 numbers are traced: 120 come straight from the pack and 95 are calculated, with live formulas.\n\nNext I can switch the theme, cost a smaller regional retail test as a fifth option, or add backup slides with the year-by-year cash model for each option.\n\nFiles are in ./deliverable/:\n- onsoo-us-entry.pptx\n- onsoo-us-entry-sources.xlsx\n- onsoo-us-entry.json"
    }
